      "content": "That feeling of futility is a very profound response to massive, systemic problems. It's true that individual actions don't fix climate change alone, which can make them feel utterly meaningless. Instead of viewing them as band-aids, consider them as acts of self-preservation or small rebellions against the apathy that allows these larger systems to continue. Sometimes, the most meaningful action is simply refusing to surrender your own spirit to the darkness.",
      "source": "target",
